Let $h,r\geq1$, put $q=p^h$, and let $(b_\ell)_{\ell\in\mathbb N^r}$ be an arbitrary family in $C$. Suppose $s\in\mathfrak m_C^r$ satisfies, for every integer $m\geq0$, $$\label{formal:root-bound}
  \limsup_{N\longrightarrow\infty}
  \left|\sum_{|\ell|\leq m} b_\ell^{1/q^N}s^\ell\right|
  \leq \|s\|^{m+1}.$$ Then, for every $k$-linear functional $\lambda:C\to k$, $$\sum_{\ell\in\mathbb N^r}\lambda(b_\ell)s^\ell=0.$$ The series in this conclusion converges, and no continuity assumption on $\lambda$ is required.

For each parameter $y$ in the height-at-least-$h$ polydisc, the formula $$\Theta_y(z)=\lim_{j\to\infty}
       P_y^{\circ j}\bigl(z^{1/Q^j}\bigr)
 \label{def:theta-limit}$$ defines a continuous natural homomorphism $$\Theta_y:\mathcal H_n(R)\longrightarrow H_y(R^{\circ\circ}).$$ Here the roots are unique because $R$ is perfect, and $P_y^{\circ j}$ denotes composition. The map $$\Phi_y:z\longmapsto
       \bigl(\Theta_y(p^{-m}z)\bigr)_{m\ge0}
 \label{def:cover-identification}$$ is a natural isomorphism $$\mathcal H_n(R)\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }
     \varprojlim_{[p]_{H_y}} H_y(R^{\circ\circ}),$$ and $\Theta_y$ is its zeroth projection. For each fixed $z\in\mathcal H_n(C)$, the function $y\mapsto\Theta_y(z)$ is analytic on the parameter polydisc.
